# .cursorrules — Nivodiya Farms ERP

## Canonical spec lives in CLAUDE.md

This project's authoritative rules, data model, migration discipline, agent
contract, and carried-forward bug-prevention rules are maintained in **CLAUDE.md**
at the repo root. Read it in full before making changes.

Do not duplicate rules here — edit CLAUDE.md and treat it as the single source
of truth. This file exists only so Cursor (if used) loads the same context.

Key reminders (full detail in CLAUDE.md):
- Build toward the variety-anchored model: Crop Cycle = variety + season = the P&L unit;
  fields are TAGS (tasks.field_id), not a hierarchy level; crop_cycle_id is nullable
  (field-prep tasks have no crop).
- Every schema change is an Alembic migration, committed and reviewed. No Supabase
  dashboard hand-edits. Watch the enum create_type=False gotcha.
- Sales and yields are NEW line-item tables; P&L is derived, not hand-maintained.
- Agent calls a FIXED tool set, never raw SQL. WhatsApp threading via short codes.
- Never surface "incident" to family — say crop cycle / फसल चक्र.
- Hindi↔English: short_description ↔ tipanni (टिप्पणी), description ↔ varnan (वर्णन). (Historically reversed — do not reintroduce.)
- Minimal-diff changes; report risk level and affected files per change.
